{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd","id":916672,"title":"A few newbie questions VTR 2nd","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-17T23:01:54-07:00","id":916672,"title":"A few newbie questions VTR 2nd","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I have recently picked up the vampire book and some other bits and pieces and will be imminently running a game but just had a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1. Suprise and reflexive. Now from what I've see suprise denies a player their action. But I've also noticed in a lot of reflexive Abilities it says 'must be aware of the attack to use'. So if you are suprised can you use things that are reflexive? Or are they denied to you? Page references would be perfect as well.<br /> <br /> 2. One of the players has come up with a build that nets him around the 25 dice to attack while denying the opponents defence. This is through a combination of high strength, Dex, weaponry, vigour and the light weapons merit which allows you to sac your defence and add it to your attack. Cheap shot to deny them their defence if his stealth attack doesn't pan out. <br /> <br /> Street fighting 3 let's him inflict the knocked down tilt which makes a person lose their action. And with this many dice he can comfortably aim for even the smallest gap in armor. And then the Kindred fighting style thrown in on top to be able to inflict lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So I firstly just wanted to make sure this was legit. Because it does seem absolutely insane being able to aim for the eye slit vs full plate still be on 20+ dice, and knock them down, blind them, and deny them defence and armor. And also how you would challenge them? Are there any merits/powers that would allow you to keep your defence when an effect says deny? <br /> <br /> 3. The merit plausible deniability. Now it says &quot;Any attempt to use a Discipline or other supernatural power to prove your character\u2019s guilt in breach of city law or Tradition automatically fails.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now does this mean if a character with auspex asks a question about this character regarding illegal going ons it won't work. Or does it only work when it is used to try and generate 'proof'? <br /> <br /> 4. And finally. I bought the god machine chronicle, VTR and a copy of the WoD core book, however I'm not sure exactly what copy of WoD I need to be using, could someone tell me how to tell which book is the most recent, or provide a link, just because I want to ensure the book I have is the correct one. <br /> <br /> Many thanks for your help<br /> Matt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T23:55:49-07:00","id":916690,"title":"","content":"1. It depends. For example, Resilience can be reflexively used to negate damage by spending blood after a wound is inflicted. There isn't really a hard and fast rule I can think of, other than if it makes sense one way or the other, go with that. That being said, I would err on the side of allowing the Reflexive action.<br /> <br /> 2. Without seeing the specific build, it's hard to say, but generally the effects of fighting styles don't stack. Using the tactics of light weaponry, a function of the Weaponry Skill, doesn't work when you're street fighting, which is a function of Brawl.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm not sure I understand the question? If you use Auspex on that character, asking if he committed a crime against the city, it would fail, yes.<br /> <br /> 4. This is admittedly a little confusing due to some behind the scenes issues: <b>The Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook</b> is the most up to date set of rules for the Storytelling system. The name change had to do with some branding issues with the previous version of WoD. However, VtR2nd includes all the basic rules you'll need to run Vampire. You can find CofD here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/168428.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\"> Chronicles of Darkness - Onyx Path Publishing | Demon: The Descent | Chronicles of Darkness | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/168428/Chronicles-of-Darkness </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chronicles of Darkness - Keep walking. Eyes straight ahead. Don&rsquo;t look back. In the shadows and between the cracks of our everyday lives hide t </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You can continue to use the old WoD core in combination with the God-Machine patch though. Not too much has changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T00:13:58-07:00","id":916693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd#post916672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Suprise and reflexive. Now from what I've see suprise denies a player their action. But I've also noticed in a lot of reflexive Abilities it says 'must be aware of the attack to use'. So if you are suprised can you use things that are reflexive? Or are they denied to you? Page references would be perfect as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, you can use a reflexive action/ability whenever it would be applicable unless something says otherwise. Surprise is one way to deny a suite of reflexive actions. Ultimately if it isn't clear remember that reflexive actions contain both &quot;automatic&quot; things like breathing, and &quot;purposeful&quot; things like moving a limited distance in a turn. Automatic stuff isn't denied lightly, while purposeful stuff is more likely to be denied.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. One of the players has come up with a build that nets him around the 25 dice to attack while denying the opponents defence. This is through a combination of high strength, Dex, weaponry, vigour and the light weapons merit which allows you to sac your defence and add it to your attack. Cheap shot to deny them their defence if his stealth attack doesn't pan out.<br /> <br /> Street fighting 3 let's him inflict the knocked down tilt which makes a person lose their action. And with this many dice he can comfortably aim for even the smallest gap in armor. And then the Kindred fighting style thrown in on top to be able to inflict lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So I firstly just wanted to make sure this was legit. Because it does seem absolutely insane being able to aim for the eye slit vs full plate still be on 20+ dice, and knock them down, blind them, and deny them defence and armor. And also how you would challenge them? Are there any merits/powers that would allow you to keep your defence when an effect says deny? </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, is someone's invested this many Merit dots into being good at hurting people, they're going to be good at it.<br /> <br /> That said, Light Weapons is a Weaponry style, which means it only works with Weaponry based attacks. Street Fighting is a Brawl style, which means it only works with Brawl based attacks. So Thrust (LW 2) and Kick 'Em While They're Down (SF 3) are not compatible moves.<br /> <br /> This tactic also requires being able to either reliably sneak attack and/or Cheap Shot. So characters that have good rolls to counter these are already in a good place to stop this in its tracks by not having their Defense removed (and if they're equally invested in defense they can Dodge with lots of dice, and can use the defensive Merits to mess up this sort of alpha strike).<br /> <br /> If they aren't surprised any character with Celerity can just use the active interrupt power to move away from this assault, and then run.<br /> <br /> There's also the ultimate trump card: friends. This character might be great against one opponent, but these sorts of tactics are going to fail fast against multiple enemies. Sacrificing your Defense - esp. in the 2e combat rules - is nigh suicidal if you're up against more than one competent opponent.<br /> <br /> There's also Predatory Auras which can be used to send someone into Wanton, using Dominate, Majesty or Nightmare, and other such tricks to just not get into combat in the first place.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, remember that the game is not about stopping inhuman monsters from being scarily powerful if they dedicate themselves to being so. It's about what happens next. How does this sort of character maintain their Humanity when they've accepted their existence as an undead killing machine? How many political bridges does their violence burn? Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. The merit plausible deniability. Now it says &quot;Any attempt to use a Discipline or other supernatural power to prove your character\u2019s guilt in breach of city law or Tradition automatically fails.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now does this mean if a character with auspex asks a question about this character regarding illegal going ons it won't work. Or does it only work when it is used to try and generate 'proof'? </div> </div> </div>Auspex doesn't generate &quot;proof&quot; The Merit protects you more from things like being Dominated into confession. All Auspex would do is allow the Auspex user to be protected via the Merit's Drawbacks. They know what the Carthian did even if they can't prove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. And finally. I bought the god machine chronicle, VTR and a copy of the WoD core book, however I'm not sure exactly what copy of WoD I need to be using, could someone tell me how to tell which book is the most recent, or provide a link, just because I want to ensure the book I have is the correct one. </div> </div> </div>Anything that says &quot;Second Edition,&quot; or &quot;Chronicles of Darkness,&quot; is the most recent (except GMC and Demon). There aren't exactly a lot of second edition books out yet. The general core (Chronicles of Darkness), Demon, Beast, VtR 2e, WtF 2e, The Pack, and Mage 2e are the current 2e books.<br /> <br /> If your copy of the WoD corebook says, &quot;World of Darkness&quot; on the cover, it's the 1e one, not the 2e one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T00:56:48-07:00","id":916708,"title":"","content":"1. Well one of the questions that came up was a sniper vs dropping prone. The sniper has suprise so the target doesn't get a turn in the first round. But we were wondering if that stopped him healing or dropping prone. <br /> <br /> 2. The Street fighting style can be used with punching daggers, but he is also looking at the shiv merit which is another work around. However the styles not combining is an interesting point, is that a written rule anywhere or an interpretation thing? <br /> <br /> I have no problem with him being incredibly powerful in combat, but that level of power at character creation does seem a little over the top, just trying to make sure I'm following the rules basically I know he can be dealt with and given challenges, but when he can turn around and 1 shot most vampires even those of a much higher level with celerity 5 full plate armor etc it just feels like something is off. Yes vs multiple opponents it becomes less scary, but 1v1 it's impossible to lose as long as he wins the initiative. Bar a terrible roll he will inflict knock down and deny them their turn. It just feels like it can beat almost any other combat build and will only get worse as he picks up celerity. <br /> <br /> 3. Well that's two conflicting answers already xD auspex gives proof to the auspex user. But not to anybody else. To me it feels like the merit is designed for use on the stand. But it's worded in a slightly awkward way... <br /> <br /> Thanks for the help so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T01:40:17-07:00","id":916728,"title":"","content":"1: Dropping prone isn't a reflexive action, it's a defensive action that's an exception to the normal order of action rules.<br /> <br /> 2: Punch daggers and shivs are weapons that can be used with Brawl. If you look at the beginning of the Merits it says specifically that Light Weapons works with Weaponry and Street Fighting works with Brawl. A shiv could be used with Light Weapons one turn, and Street Fighting the next, but not both at the same time.<br /> <br /> Can you describe how he's both getting 25+ dice, and winning initiative so easily, esp. at start? Heck, how is he even managing all these Merits at start?<br /> <br /> Also, if he doesn't get a surprise attack, Celerity trumps this via active use, even if he'd have the higher initiative without active Celerity use. The Celerity user can just interrupt him to hit first or run away. And Celerity passively adds to Initiative, which is a very mathematically lopsided roll off. What looks like a small edge in Initiative is generally a lot statistically.<br /> <br /> 3:<br /> <br /> Well, Auspex 1-3 doesn't give proof in any shape. It gives impressions. Auspex 5 isn't relevant. Auspex 4 is the only real sticking point of whether or not it might be &quot;proof.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T02:28:08-07:00","id":916741,"title":"","content":"Iirc he has 4 Str. 3 vigour. 5 weaponry. So there's 12 dice. Then 4 Dex 5 athletics. Giving him 9 defence. Which he sacrifices to put him to 21 dice to attack. Spending a Willpower is what tips it harder. And his initiative is pretty high too. Not auto high win but high enough that he has a good chance of acting first if his stealth fails.<br /> <br /> Also shiv is MAY use your Brawl for them there's no requirement to use weaponry or Brawl skills for either of the styles. And light weaponry is any 'one handed weapon with damage of two or less' which definitly works with shiv. Which is allowed with street fighting.<br /> <br /> Merit wise 3 points in street fighting gets you knock down. 2 in light gets you sac your defence and add it to your attack and 1 point gets you shiv","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T08:30:20-07:00","id":916850,"title":"","content":"In general, Vampire fights are slapfights; most of damage sources will deal Bashing Damage, which in turn allows very easy regeneration and tilt removal. Your typical Vampire brawl might look brutal, but unless someone flips out, it will probably will end with both sides deciding to stop this shit now because they are going low on blood. Most of these tricks would be relatively pointless against vampires, because again, you being blinded isn't much of a problem if the wound that blinded you is 1 Bashing damage that you are healing anyway. <br /> The thing you should be wary about is the fact that he can ignore the basic assumption of vampire combat and go straight for Lethal. It has following effects:<br /> - It, effectively, skips a whole health bar. Normal vampires have to punch through Bashing Health Boxes, which is about 7-9 health; it gives a lot of time for damage control by spending blood to regenerate, and makes conflicts relatively low on lethality<br /> - By jumping straight to Lethal, he fucks up the basic assumption of regeneration being able to match or even outpace the damage dealt. It cuts their healing in half (you get 2 Bashing damage healed for one Blood Point; you get one lethal per blood point), which will mean that he will be able to outdamage their healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T09:51:06-07:00","id":916878,"title":"","content":"This build seems cripplingly overspecialized. Challenging him should be very easy, just put him in any situation that can't easily be resolved with violence. Even in violent situations, a character with a single dot of Celerity can just spend a point of Vitae to interrupt his action by running away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:11:05-07:00","id":916884,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah as I have said I have no issues with him being a complete monster in a fight, I will find other ways to challenge his character. It just felt like he was too powerful. So wanted to make sure it was legit within the rules. He is playing a Kindred killer he is well aware I'm running demons and werewolves and hunters in this campaign. I do worry his plan is mass diablrie, which is why I wanted to confirm how the merit plausible deniability actually worked with regards to if other players could auspex the information out but not use powers to prove to the masses in a court of law situation. <br /> <br /> Is there any way to defend against effects that would reduce your defence to 0? There seem to be a few things that do it but very little to protect against it. To me it seems to be the big unbalancing part of the system as no matter how much you invest in a perfect defence a two point merit (cheap shot) and winning on a Dex + sub vs Wits + Composure roll completely eliminates them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:17:44-07:00","id":916887,"title":"","content":"If you worry that he is planning mass diablerie, why won't you ask him if he is planning mass diablerie, and then explain to him that you might not be comfortable with running a mass diablerie chronicle? Communication is the key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:05:55-07:00","id":916913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916741#post916741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not auto high win but high enough that he has a good chance of acting first if his stealth fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>His Stealth is going to fail a lot... at start how does he have any dots left for serious investment in it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also shiv is MAY use your Brawl for them there's no requirement to use weaponry or Brawl skills for either of the styles. And light weaponry is any 'one handed weapon with damage of two or less' which definitly works with shiv. Which is allowed with street fighting. </div> </div> </div>Light weapon also says, &quot;Your character is trained with small hand-to-hand weapons which favor finesse over raw power.&quot; which shiv and Street Fighting most certainly don't.<br /> <br /> Street Fighting also says, &quot;These maneuvers may only be used unarmed, or with weapons capable of using the Brawl Skill, such as punch daggers, or weapons concealed with the Shiv Merit (above).&quot; So it pretty clearly only works with Brawl attacks.<br /> <br /> If you want to allow Light Weapon 2 to work with Street Fighting 3, that's your call. I'd say it's ambiguous at best in the rules; but clearly not the intent. As well, removing the +9 dice from Thrust stacked with Kick 'Em While They're Down removes this from being any sort of problem. If the rules aren't 100% clear, and one reading results in something that doesn't seem intended and is clearly not fun for the game (which means not being fun for you) don't allow it. He's a combat monster that can devastate enemies without trying to sneak an iffy combo in.<br /> <br /> In either case, this isn't a valid starting level character anyway. He'd need Athletics 5, Weaponry 5, and Brawl 2. That's 12 dots in Physical Skills, when you only start with 11 max. And that leaves him with zero Stealth to stealth people with, and zero Larceny to hide weapons on himself (negating a lot of the point of the Shiv Merit). If he's maxing out for Cheap Shot, he's invested all his Social Skills in Subterfuge and Streetwise (required for Street Fighting).<br /> <br /> As Charlaquin noted, this is an extremely one-trick pony character at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916884#post916884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is playing a Kindred killer he is well aware I'm running demons and werewolves and hunters in this campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>A decently combat focused werewolf has a lot of tricks that will laugh this off. Demons can easily stop it from starting. It's a bit of a waste to go the &quot;super hard combat monster,&quot; as a vampire with other supernaturals in the mix. Vampires are no push overs in individual combat, but it's not their strongest area.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do worry his plan is mass diablrie, which is why I wanted to confirm how the merit plausible deniability actually worked with regards to if other players could auspex the information out but not use powers to prove to the masses in a court of law situation. </div> </div> </div>How is he going to earn Carthian Status enough to even get such protections if he's a violent socipath that cares more about eating other vampires than politics? He's got to earn that Carthian Status 3 somehow before even getting to learning Plausible Deniability. What's stopping him from getting offed before he gets that far? It's not like he's got the skills or friends to do much if the other locals find his murder-happy ways unsavory and have him killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any way to defend against effects that would reduce your defence to 0? </div> </div> </div>Supernatural armors that you can't make called shots around. Any power that reduces damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me it seems to be the big unbalancing part of the system as no matter how much you invest in a perfect defence a two point merit (cheap shot) and winning on a Dex + sub vs Wits + Composure roll completely eliminates them. </div> </div> </div>Cheap Shot has to win, and each time you use it, that gets less and less likely. It also doesn't stop the other character from acting like a sneak attack does. You're still open to being attacked, or them trying to run away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:33:41-07:00","id":916922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916887#post916887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you worry that he is planning mass diablerie, why won't you ask him if he is planning mass diablerie, and then explain to him that you might not be comfortable with running a mass diablerie chronicle? Communication is the key.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this. Any time I read &quot;I'm worried about my player(s)...&quot; my immediate reaction is why are you talking this concern up with a bunch of strangers on the internet instead of the player(s)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:42:31-07:00","id":916927,"title":"","content":"CofD combat is <i>violent</i>. Arm Wreck, blinding, magic powers, retainer/familar swarms (or Protean insect swarms), mind control. These are all devistating tactics. My personal favorite tactic at the moment is from my Acolyte Khaibit. Use Gaze of the Gorgon, negating the need for a eyesight with the free Gift from the bloodline. I'm at 16 dice without willpower (Presence 4, Occult 4, +2 specialty, Cruac 3, +3 from Mantle of Amorous Fire); the opponent rolls Stamina + BP, subtracting my successes. Each success is a point of aggravated damage, and turns one limb to stone; Resilience might prevent the damage, but not the turning-to-stone limbs. That is going to really put a wrench in any combat tactics. And the best part? I haven't even used my action - just opened my eyes to meet someone's gaze. And this isn't a combat-focused character.<br /> <br /> Combat, in my experience, is rately about who's got the larger dice pools. Its all about <i>breaking</i> the other person first. If you can Arm Wreck or Blind someone, they're screwed. Attack from Celerity distance with a bow for staking. Dominate someone and force them into a docile state. This isn't D&amp;D and a struggle to reduce someone's HP total to zero. This isn't a heroic battle. This is fighting dirty and hurting others before they can hurt you. Its about breaking someone's will to fight. I don't honestly care if a player has a dice pool of 45 with Vigor 5. That's not enough to consistantly take down a vampire with 2 stamina and 1 Resilience in one round. Because, I promise you, any decently combat vampire will destroy the ability of that 50-dice character to fight back in the next turn.<br /> <br /> Like Charlaquin said, this is cripplingly overspecialized to do one thing, and one thing only. Like WHW said, vampire combat with this character's specialty is basically &quot;slap fight&quot; territory since everything is bashing damage. Vampire combat, at its most brutal, involves staking, grapples, fire, Dominates, Obfuscates/Celerity evasions, and other one-sided, heavy handed methods. A starting Protean specialist can turn themselves into a swarm of insects - you can't beat that with just a shiv. Your options are to outrun the swarm, use magic, or be bitten into torpor. The character has no defense or ability to fight against anyone other than another swordsman, and even then? Don't mess with Daeva using Enfeebling aura, Vigor and a stake. <br /> <br /> Frankly, &quot;challenging&quot; this character would be difficult because I would likely end up one sidedly slapping this character down. My vampires believe that, short of Kindred Dueling, there's no real reason to go after each other with guns or blades. You go for the magic, you go for staking, you go for grapples with bites to tear the other's throat out, you go for mind control, or you just Celerity/Obfuscate away and avoid fights altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T11:44:34-07:00","id":916929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916884#post916884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to defend against effects that would reduce your defence to 0? There seem to be a few things that do it but very little to protect against it. To me it seems to be the big unbalancing part of the system as no matter how much you invest in a perfect defence a two point merit (cheap shot) and winning on a Dex + sub vs Wits + Composure roll completely eliminates them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly? Acute Senses (a one point merit) is a very strong ways of raising your Wits+Composure roll to very high levels to the point that winning that Dex+Subterfuge roll is going to be very difficult. Vampires aren't known for their dull senses, after all, and there's no known way to raise a Dex+Subterfuge roll in VtR. This should be reflected among your NPCs as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-18-2016, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T12:56:27-07:00","id":916952,"title":"","content":"Well, Physical Intensity can boost Dex, and all the standard stuff (Professional Training, Area of Expertise, etc.) for boosting Stealth/Subterfuge, but there's also Danger Sense, Trained Observer, Kindred Senses + Auspex, and so on for the other side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:11:59-07:00","id":916956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916913#post916913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His Stealth is going to fail a lot... at start how does he have any dots left for serious investment in it?<br /> <br /> In either case, this isn't a valid starting level character anyway. He'd need Athletics 5, Weaponry 5, and Brawl 2. That's 12 dots in Physical Skills, when you only start with 11 max. And that leaves him with zero Stealth to stealth people with, and zero Larceny to hide weapons on himself (negating a lot of the point of the Shiv Merit). If he's maxing out for Cheap Shot, he's invested all his Social Skills in Subterfuge and Streetwise (required for Street Fighting).<br /> <br /> How is he going to earn Carthian Status enough to even get such protections if he's a violent socipath that cares more about eating other vampires than politics? He's got to earn that Carthian Status 3 somehow before even getting to learning Plausible Deniability. What's stopping him from getting offed before he gets that far? It's not like he's got the skills or friends to do much if the other locals find his murder-happy ways unsavory and have him killed.<br /> <br /> Cheap Shot has to win, and each time you use it, that gets less and less likely. It also doesn't stop the other character from acting like a sneak attack does. You're still open to being attacked, or them trying to run away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have his character sheet to hand but im his feats were along the lines of: Street fighting 3, light 2, cheap 2, shiv 1, defensive combat 1 (allowing him to use weaponry instead of athletics).<br /> <br /> This frees up the points to give him a good stealth capability. With 4 in Dex too he should sneak past most people.<br /> <br /> And he plays the long game. He isn't a stupid player. If he kills he will do so in a controlled way. He is not a trigger happy murder hobo, his character may look that way but he may be a sociopath. But he won't be a stupid one. Climbing up the ladders of Carthian won't really be an issue assuming he doesn't mess up big time. He won't go on his killing sprees until he has established himself in a position he can do so safely. <br /> <br /> And I get cheap shot has downsides. It was more curious if there were ways to not be butchered by the 'drop defence to 0' side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:41:22-07:00","id":916970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916956#post916956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have his character sheet to hand but im his feats were along the lines of: Street fighting 3, light 2, cheap 2, shiv 1, defensive combat 1 (allowing him to use weaponry instead of athletics).</div> </div> </div> </div> Those are all merits. We're talking about Physical Skills. You get 11/7/4 dots to distribute in skills. If we're looking at 5Weaponery and 5 Athletics, that leaves one dot left for Stealth, and none for Larceny. Hardly a competent sneak. Frankly, this character sounds rather dubious. We're talking starting character, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This frees up the points to give him a good stealth capability. With 4 in Dex too he should sneak past most people. </div> </div> </div> Not how it works. First of all, there's lots of times that you'll have environmental penalties factored in. Usually, that's against the stealth character in question. Secondly, Wits+Composure, the usual roll, is actually rather high for most people. Lets say 5 dice. Even with 4 dice in dex and a 3 in stealth, that's only 7 dice. That's lots of room for pure luck to have a huge sway in the outcome. I would not take that as a granted at any point. Especially when we're talking about Kindred Senses being higher than the average mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And he plays the long game. He isn't a stupid player. If he kills he will do so in a controlled way. </div> </div> </div> In short, a sociopath killer. That's going to be good for his Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Climbing up the ladders of Carthian won't really be an issue assuming he doesn't mess up big time. He won't go on his killing sprees until he has established himself in a position he can do so safely. </div> </div> </div> Climbing the &quot;ladder&quot; of the Carthians should actually be difficult for this character. Carthians run on the &quot;popularity&quot; scale. And, to be frank, this guy is super focused on the combat side. By all rights, he should be lacking the charisma and the social skill sets in order to make swaying the population of the Carthians difficult. Simply put, don't give them the benefit of the doubt. Require the use of social merits and Social Maneuvering. Require favors that don't involve combat as an answer.<br /> <br /> Violence can solve almost any problem, but it often creates more problems than it solves in the process. Vampire is a social game. It revolves are the politics and asking the question &quot;What are you willing to do to survive?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I get cheap shot has downsides. It was more curious if there were ways to not be butchered by the 'drop defence to 0' side of things. </div> </div> </div> Resilience, Celerity to move out of sword range, disappearing with Obfuscate, Protean to shift to a different form, have a ghoul retainer step in front of you, put something else between the two of you, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T13:52:44-07:00","id":916974,"title":"","content":"A classical Sherrif with two handed sword, appropiate style and some disciplines will be almost unkillable for this character, btw, without having to invest half as much as that dude does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:58:28-07:00","id":917092,"title":"","content":"It sounds like he builds a purely combat character then uses his own IRL Intelligence, Wits, Presence and Manipulation to play it. You can shut him down easy by making him roll to see if his character is smart, charismatic, or finess-y enough to know or do what he is attempting to.<br /> <br /> He will be powerful at assassination in combat but if he's too &quot;dumb&quot; in character to plan or manipulate the conditions for the assassination, then it's not going to do him much good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T22:20:38-07:00","id":917187,"title":"","content":"The upcoming Hurt Locker addresses the fighting merits question. This would be a draft but indicates the official line of thought. So my question would be explain how using light weapons and street fighting works at the same time (to the player)? It won't work if it can't get passed the first rule.<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Stacking Fighting Merits</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can you use more than one Fighting Style maneuver or other Merit in a single attack? Sometimes. The following rules apply.</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>If nobody can explain how the maneuvers would stack in the story, it doesn\u2019t work. The player needs to describe an action that brings them together. Your two pistol backflip headlock\u2019s probably going to sound dumb\u2014unless you can somehow make it sound <i>amazing</i>.</li> <li>The required equipment or other circumstances for all maneuvers used must be present.</li> <li>You can\u2019t stack Fighting Merits that penalize one of your character\u2019s traits more than once, or impose the same disadvantage more than once. For example, you cannot stack two Merits that lower Defence.</li> <li>You can\u2019t stack maneuvers that use different dice pools, unless changing the dice pool is a benefit the Merit specifically confers. For example, you can use Fighting Finesse with maneuvers that require Strength + Weaponry, and they\u2019ll use Dexterity + Weaponry instead, but you can\u2019t combine a Merit that uses Weaponry with one that uses Brawl.</li> <li>When stacked maneuvers provide the same benefit, the higher of the two apply. All disadvantages apply (though remember that you can\u2019t stack maneuvers that impose the same disadvantage twice). Note that when two maneuvers provide the same result by different means, they <i>do</i> stack, so the Rote benefit (re-roll failed dice) does stack with bonus dice.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T01:24:48-07:00","id":917235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916970#post916970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Those are all merits. We're talking about Physical Skills. You get 11/7/4 dots to distribute in skills. If we're looking at 5Weaponery and 5 Athletics, that leaves one dot left for Stealth, and none for Larceny. Hardly a competent sneak. Frankly, this character sounds rather dubious. We're talking starting character, right?<br /> <br /> Not how it works. First of all, there's lots of times that you'll have environmental penalties factored in. Usually, that's against the stealth character in question. Secondly, Wits+Composure, the usual roll, is actually rather high for most people. Lets say 5 dice. Even with 4 dice in dex and a 3 in stealth, that's only 7 dice. That's lots of room for pure luck to have a huge sway in the outcome. I would not take that as a granted at any point. Especially when we're talking about Kindred Senses being higher than the average mortal.<br /> <br /> In short, a sociopath killer. That's going to be good for his Humanity.<br /> <br /> Climbing the &amp;quot;ladder&amp;quot; of the Carthians should actually be difficult for this character. Carthians run on the &amp;quot;popularity&amp;quot; scale. And, to be frank, this guy is super focused on the combat side. By all rights, he should be lacking the charisma and the social skill sets in order to make swaying the population of the Carthians difficult. Simply put, don't give them the benefit of the doubt. Require the use of social merits and Social Maneuvering. Require favors that don't involve combat as an answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The defensive combat merit allows him to use weaponry instead of athletics to determine defence. So that has freed up 5 skill points for him to put into stealth. <br /> <br /> And it's less the stealth being powerful. It's that he has multiple points of success. Firstly he can attempt to stealth. He should usually have the advantage here bar environmental penalties. Should that fail he then has sucker punch where it's likely he will have the advantage again. Across the two instances of completely denying defence this gives him good odds of achieving it rather than leaving it to a single roll. Obviously not guarenteed. But good odds nonetheless. <br /> <br /> Then with their 0 defence. He rolls 20+ dice. Netting on average 7 successes. Adding his vigour of 3, and weapon damage of 1. This equates to an 11 lethal damage opening round. Enough to OTK generally.<br /> <br /> I've warned him about humanity. And I won't be making climbing the ladder easy by any stretch. This is simply where I feel his character will go. It may not and he may take an entirely different route or be taken out before he makes it there or not make it there at all. All I am doing is trying to ensure I have the rules correct before encountering the situation. The main one being does auspex work against plausible deniability. However I does seem like it's a GMs call as people seem divided on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=916974#post916974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A classical Sherrif with two handed sword, appropiate style and some disciplines will be almost unkillable for this character, btw, without having to invest half as much as that dude does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you care to elaborate on this? Because I'm looking at the two handed weapon style and not really seeing any impact it would have at all if I'm honest. Generally it would come down to if his stealth got off. And if that failed him winning initiative. if he achieved either of those things I'm struggling to come up with a core build (diciplines aside) that can even survive the initial attack let alone give him a challenge.<br /> <br /> Obviously he is a combat monster 90% of things won't stand a chance against him. But it would be nice to have a rival who could at least give him a run for his money. If it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:45:10-07:00","id":917266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917235#post917235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that has freed up 5 skill points for him to put into stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three, he still needs Athletics 2 for Light Weaponry, and his Brawl score is still painfully low if he's going to rely on Street Fighting.<br /> <br /> Dex 4/Stealth 3 is going to fall fairly flat against anyone built against sneak attacks. Wits + Composure of 6, Danger Sense is ups it to 8, Trained Observer tosses in 8- or 9-again depend on rating. Acute Senses for a vampire adds BP to the equation. So 6 Merit dots, and less investment in Attributes and he's not sneaking up on anyone with a watch dog in the party.<br /> <br /> You keep insisting he &quot;should have the advantage.&quot; There's no reason to assume this. He only has the advantage if you let him by never putting him up against someone that's even a bit invested in not getting sneak attacked/sucker punched (which are things vampires generally like to avoid considering it's the easiest way to ruin their night).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Across the two instances of completely denying defence this gives him good odds of achieving it rather than leaving it to a single roll. </div> </div> </div>You're still leaving active use of Celerity out of the equation here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you care to elaborate on this? Because I'm looking at the two handed weapon style and not really seeing any impact it would have at all if I'm honest. </div> </div> </div>It's a nice counter to Cheap Shot. If he gets close, not only does he takes damage, but suffers a flat -X penalty to Defense for the turn, leaving him open to Bring the Pain and a flat penalty to everything for the next turn.<br /> <br /> So this combat monster tries to close in for a cheap shot. The sheriff pops on Celerity for an interrupt and Vigor for extra damage. The combat monser's 9 Defense drops to 6, takes 1 damage. The sheriff attacks with his 3 damage 9 again sword boosted to say, 5 via Vigor, sacrificing his defense for Bring the Pain, and gets 2 successes to hit. Since he dots 7 damage, our combat monster (who doesn't seem to have a lot of Stamina to have all that Strength and Dex) is at least in -2 wound penalties (and potentially in a lot of trouble if the sheriff has Kindred Dueling to make that lethal). So that's -9 dice on the first attack, -9 dice on the Cheap shot roll, and -9 dice on whatever he wants to try the next round (and he needs to withstand the strong possibility of going second).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously he is a combat monster 90% of things won't stand a chance against him. But it would be nice to have a rival who could at least give him a run for his money. If it exists. </div> </div> </div>He's not actually that well built of a combat monster. He's ridiculously easy to beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T03:50:39-07:00","id":917276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917266#post917266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three, he still needs Athletics 2 for Light Weaponry, and his Brawl score is still painfully low if he's going to rely on Street Fighting.<br /> <br /> Dex 4/Stealth 3 is going to fall fairly flat against anyone built against sneak attacks. Wits + Composure of 6, Danger Sense is ups it to 8, Trained Observer tosses in 8- or 9-again depend on rating. Acute Senses for a vampire adds BP to the equation. So 6 Merit dots, and less investment in Attributes and he's not sneaking up on anyone with a watch dog in the party.<br /> <br /> You keep insisting he &amp;quot;should have the advantage.&amp;quot; There's no reason to assume this. He only has the advantage if you let him by never putting him up against someone that's even a bit invested in not getting sneak attacked/sucker punched (which are things vampires generally like to avoid considering it's the easiest way to ruin their night).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're still leaving active use of Celerity out of the equation here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's a nice counter to Cheap Shot. If he gets close, not only does he takes damage, but suffers a flat -X penalty to Defense for the turn, leaving him open to Bring the Pain and a flat penalty to everything for the next turn.<br /> <br /> So this combat monster tries to close in for a cheap shot. The sheriff pops on Celerity for an interrupt and Vigor for extra damage. The combat monser's 9 Defense drops to 6, takes 1 damage. The sheriff attacks with his 3 damage 9 again sword boosted to say, 5 via Vigor, sacrificing his defense for Bring the Pain, and gets 2 successes to hit. Since he dots 7 damage, our combat monster (who doesn't seem to have a lot of Stamina to have all that Strength and Dex) is at least in -2 wound penalties (and potentially in a lot of trouble if the sheriff has Kindred Dueling to make that lethal). So that's -9 dice on the first attack, -9 dice on the Cheap shot roll, and -9 dice on whatever he wants to try the next round (and he needs to withstand the strong possibility of going second).</div> </div> </div> </div>I say should have the advantage because he has an above average dice pool. Therefore on average he should have advantage. Against a notice bunny obviously he will have a much harder time.<br /> <br /> 7 dice isn't that low. Especially at creation. And if that person has invested that heavily into notice and not into combat he can just walk up to him and hit him instead. The overall outcome is the same.<br /> <br /> And say that gives him a 50% chance at succeeding/failing his stealth against the average vampire. Then should that fail he has a roughly 50% chance of succeeding the sucker punch. Compounded that's a 75% chance of achieving a OTK if he is able to get his attack off. Yes I know he isn't guarenteed to OTK but with that many dice to attack with he should do pretty alright.<br /> <br /> And celerity is only a hard counter until he picks up his first dot in it, and in all honesty he could comfortably drop down to vigour 2 and pick up celerity at creation without much of a negative impact to his build it would be a lot more optimised. At which point it's another chance area. But celerity also can't be used in response to a suprise attack. So there is already a 50% chance of him just auto-winning against this sheriff. Followed by a 25% chance to auto win if the fight starts without suprise (50% on Celerity and 50% on sucker punch) a fight that could go either way. So vs this Sherrif he is already beginning with roughly a 62.5% chance of winning. Followed by a fight that could then go either way really. If he doesn't get his OTK set up he has a defence of 9. So pretty solid. The fight at this point could go either way really. But unless I'm missing a lot of things this sheriff seems like he would be a pretty easy target. <br /> <br /> Of course this is all assuming he is the one targeting the sheriff. And not the Sherrif hunting him. But this Sherrif doesn't exactly seem like a stealthy assassination type.<br /> <br /> I know it's not unbeatable. And there is more than one way to skin a cat after all. But I'm looking at combat. I'm also not saying it's the best most optimised build out there. Simply that it seemed pretty obscene at a first glance so I'm attempting to wrap my head around what to expect in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T05:58:46-07:00","id":917305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917235#post917235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The defensive combat merit allows him to use weaponry instead of athletics to determine defence. So that has freed up 5 skill points for him to put into stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div> So he doesn't even have Athletics? Wow, that's pretty bad - this character is open bait for a sneak attack by opponents, or even someone that disarms him. Anything the PCs do, NPCs can do back. Also, as H.A. pointed out, there are requirements for the merits he picked that take up more room.<br /> <br /> Even more notably, I didn't see Quick Draw there. That means that, in event of combat happening, your player is going to spend a turn to draw his weapon. Even if he (I'm assuming he at this point, appologies if wrong) does have Quick Draw, he can't use it until his turn; that means that anyone acting before his turn gets to use his lowered Defense, since he doesn't have his weapon drawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's less the stealth being powerful. It's that he has multiple points of success. Firstly he can attempt to stealth. He should usually have the advantage here bar environmental penalties. Should that fail he then has sucker punch where it's likely he will have the advantage again. Across the two instances of completely denying defence this gives him good odds of achieving it rather than leaving it to a single roll. Obviously not guarenteed. But good odds nonetheless. </div> </div> </div> Only in a white room with no other features, situations perfectly aligned for him. White rooms are unrealistic. You're going to be in rooms with chairs and tables, or people in the way, or garbage in an alley, etc. This is where that lack of Athetics comes into play - how you going to -get- to the enemy in your turn?<br /> <br /> Anyone with a single dot of Celerity or Obfuscate are going to readily hand this guy his own arse on a silver platter in the fields he supposedly excells in. He's going to be going up against Mehket watchdogs, multiple ghouls who all get rolls, animals who get to rely on scent, and more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then with their 0 defence. He rolls 20+ dice. Netting on average 7 successes. Adding his vigour of 3, and weapon damage of 1. This equates to an 11 lethal damage opening round. Enough to OTK generally. </div> </div> </div> No. That's 11 Bashing. Vampires only suffer bashing from mundane weapons. That's only enough to put someone with the Small merit and Stamina 1 into torpor. Pretty rare combination. Even with Vigor 5, we're talking 14 bashing damage, which isn't even enough to put someone with Stamina 3 down, let alone anyone built for actual fighting. Iron Skin also applies as armor here, since all weapons are bashing by default.<br /> <br /> You need Kindred Dueling 3 to make regular attacks into Lethal damage, and you need to use an edged weapon - a shiv is not an edged weapon. Other options for dealing Lethal to vampires include using Theban's Vitae Lash, Cruac rituals, or Protean claws. This character is not built for any of those four, which means all his damage with his weapon is going to be Bashing. At best, he can start carrying around wooden stakes and go that route for fighting against other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you care to elaborate on this? Because I'm looking at the two handed weapon style and not really seeing any impact it would have at all if I'm honest. </div> </div> </div> Heh. That's kind of the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally it would come down to if his stealth got off. And if that failed him winning initiative. if he achieved either of those things I'm struggling to come up with a core build (diciplines aside) that can even survive the initial attack let alone give him a challenge. </div> </div> </div> Winning stealth against multiple opponents (relying on situations where you can actually stealth!) isn't a given, winning intiative against Celerity users is laughable.<br /> <br /> And why are you trying to discount Disciplines? Magic powers &gt; mortal abilities. Fighting Styles were huge in 1e, sure. In 2e, magic powers are devistating. You're shooting yourself in the foot when Disciplines are a major part of any vampire's arsenal. I mean, hells. You're freely adding in Vigor to the mix, for him, but not for anyone else? One of these is not like the other.<br /> <br /> But if you want mortal abilities? Fine. One option is high initiative, a weapon that can break bones, called shot to the character's main arm. Arm Wreck the guy, he drops the weapon, can't fight anymore. Game, set match. Tilts are brutal. Another option is the Animal or Retainer Swarm - this guy is crap against multiple opponents. There's the staking expert. Grapple-frenzy builds. Snipers. Kindred Dueling with Heavy Weapons FS and Vigor - Warding Stance gives weapon (+vigor) as armor rating; when coupled with actual armor and Resilience, we can reduce damage dealt by your PC to a pitance, and hit back hard enough to torpor the person in question with one hit. I mentioned Iron Skin before. Several of us have mentioned ways to boost perception rolls, which negates the stealth / cheap shot attacks to nothing, leaving the character without their ability to negate defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously he is a combat monster 90% of things won't stand a chance against him. But it would be nice to have a rival who could at least give him a run for his money. If it exists. </div> </div> </div> No.... most <i>mortals</i> won't stand a chance. Most vampires will laugh this guy off. Same with Rahu werewolves in Gauru form. Mages and changelings have a multitude of powers that would prevent him from getting close enough to do anything. Any combat demon would have Just Bruised, reducing all damage down to 1L. Beasts are a varied lot, depending on their Atavisms, Nightmares, and current Satiety levels, so that depends on individual builds. And I think an appropriately built Lost Boy mortal could handle him as well.<br /> <br /> There are also multiple fighting styles in Secrets of the Covenant that actually undermine this guy's one trick. Specifically, Temple Guardian for CotC and the Impailed FS for the Ordo would actually benefit from fighting this guy than suffer penalties.<br /> <br /> I said it before, and others have said it. This guy is not really that good. He's a one trick pony that's not built to take the innate magical properties of supernaturals into account. He needs at least two attacks before putting anyone into torpor, which leaves him wide open for being hit back (sacrificed Defense), majorly open against multiple oponents, mind controlled, sneak attacked himself (there are two clans with Obfuscate!), staked, hit with magical powers, and more.<br /> <br /> He's trying for an assassin build, but lacks the actual ability to pull it off reliably. Combat is rarely one turn and a one-on-one situation. Anything other than an ideal scenario for this guy, and he's toast. He has to win <i>every time</i>, but all he needs is one bad roll and he's FUBAR.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917276#post917276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 dice isn't that low. Especially at creation. And if that person has invested that heavily into notice and not into combat he can just walk up to him and hit him instead. The overall outcome is the same.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its low enough that its unreliable against multiple opponents who can spot him. One good roll for the opponents, and its all over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And say that gives him a 50% chance at succeeding/failing his stealth against the average vampire. Then should that fail he has a roughly 50% chance of succeeding the sucker punch. Compounded that's a 75% chance of achieving a OTK if he is able to get his attack off. Yes I know he isn't guarenteed to OTK but with that many dice to attack with he should do pretty alright. </div> </div> </div> Except that he's not going to be going against &quot;average vampire.&quot; He's going against vampires with their cotiries behind them, with animal retainers, with combat experience, with rituals and magic. As well, he's going to be in a party against opponents also in a cotorie - and the entire PC group aren't stealth experts. He's going to be going against a unique character with actual experience dealing with hunters, fellow vampires, and other things.<br /> <br /> There's no such thing as an &quot;average&quot; vampire. You can have stereotypes, but there's enough wide range of abilities that you're just making blanket assumptions. The stereotypical Ventrue and Gangrel still will have plenty of Resilience to shrug off lots of damage. Stereotypical Daeva are going to have lots of Celerity and Vigor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And celerity is only a hard counter until he picks up his first dot in it, </div> </div> </div> But he hasn't. And even if he does? That just means a Clash of Wills - someone with more dots or higher BP is generally going to beat him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So there is already a 50% chance of him just auto-winning against this sheriff. </div> </div> </div> Hardly. Sheriffs are generally ancillae level or higher. We're talking lots of experience and training, including high perception pools, combat skill, and general investigation powers. And then, there's that pesky Resilience a Sheriff likely has, as well as at least a BP of 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Followed by a 25% chance to auto win if the fight starts without suprise (50% on Celerity and 50% on sucker punch) a fight that could go either way. So vs this Sherrif he is already beginning with roughly a 62.5% chance of winning. Followed by a fight that could then go either way really. If he doesn't get his OTK set up he has a defence of 9. So pretty solid. The fight at this point could go either way really. But unless I'm missing a lot of things this sheriff seems like he would be a pretty easy target. </div> </div> </div> You're throwing out numbers that won't add up in reality. Remember, all the PC needs is one unlucky roll to be screwed. 25% chance of failure when failure means you're screwed to the point of getting a new PC? That's TERRIBLE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'm looking at combat. I'm also not saying it's the best most optimised build out there. Simply that it seemed pretty obscene at a first glance so I'm attempting to wrap my head around what to expect in combat. </div> </div> </div>Honestly? I think you're borrowing trouble, as well as you seem to have a few misunderstanding with rule changes from 1e to 2e.<br /> <br /> Lets set up a scenario here. Nomad cotorie comes to town, makes a mess in your cotorie's territory. What happens? The nomads set up in an abandoned house of some kind - infiltrating this haven, even if its temporary, is going to be bumping into penalties from the Safe Place merit. As well, haven is going to boost Kindred Senses. Already, that's a huge bonus to notice your PC sneak; if we assume 3 dots in each merit, along with 3 nomads plus ghoul escorts, that's still enough to put the dice to favor the nomads. If the PC moves on his own, he's screwed in a 3-on-1 battle, since he loses all his Defenses to pull off his trick. And that's still not counting the ghouls.<br /> <br /> Therefore, lets say he doesn't move alone, and goes in with the PC cotorie. That means we're relying entirely on Cheap Shot for removing defense, and winning Initiative, and dealing enough damage for a one-hit-one-kill mindset, and that there aren't any people who will use Disciplines in combat, and that they won't have someone just Obfuscate the group and set up a counter ambush.<br /> <br /> Okay, lets just say that attacking the haven is a bad idea. Attempts to moltov the place are met by ghouls with fire extinguishers and cops and witnesses; bad for PCs as well. So, lets move on to something else - waiting for the nomads to leave the haven and do their thing. That means tracking them by car without being spotted, or in crowded populations. Getting a sneak attack with a shiv here is possible, but also very noticable if something goes wrong with lots of witnesses.<br /> <br /> And lets say we finally get the ideal situation where the nomads grab people into an abandoned ally. They're distracted, haven't caught the tail (a stretch to assume in the first place). The PC in question gets to perfectly pull off his attack. However, its only 11 Bashing damage. The nomad still stands, and rides the wave. Immediately attempts a grapple; handily succeeds without Defense in the way. With equal dots of Vigor, appropriate grappling FS, and superior dots of Brawl as well as frenzy bonus? We're talking a onesided contest where our shiv master is at the mercy of the grappler.<br /> <br /> No matter how you spin this rather common scenario, the shiv-specialist is kind of lame without some very luck rolls. Hells. In the ideal situation above, if he used a stake instead of shiv? He would have won. This doesn't even include our nomads using Disciplines beyond Vigor. Imagine Dominating the PC in question to attack his allies. Or putting him under Majesty's sway. There are reflexive uses of Nightmare to remove one from the board. No defense against counter-ambushes. <br /> <br /> Now, lets pit our shiv master against a Rahu werewolf. We'll even white room this to let the shiv master go first and have all the advantages. He attacks, gets all the perfect situation. 11 lethal damage! Our werewolf has reflexively shifted into Gauru for extra life and has extra life (automatically gained at char gen for all Rahu with Purity 2). Its not enough to kill our Rahu. Start of his turn, all damage heals. Our werewolf uses Efficent Killer (prerequisite: Purity 2, two dot merit) to deal his full dice pool as automatic damage with a bite - that's at least 10 lethal damage back, not counting any Gifts or other merits. Shiv master falls to torpor. Winner - Rahu.<br /> <br /> I could go on. And these are basic starting characters, nothing twinked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-19-2016, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:17:40-07:00","id":917332,"title":"","content":"Wow this is a long thread. <br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned that defense is the lower of wits and dex? I noticed that they kept saying +4 from dex, but that means your wits would have to be 4-5 ...<br /> <br /> I am going to agree with most everyone else, fighting styles, for the most do not stack.<br /> <br /> If he really doesn't have athletics and needs to use the lower of wits which could be 4 .. His defense would be 4 ... So that's not as<br /> Many dice to drop and add to attacking <br /> <br /> Next ... You should really post his character sheet instead of all these hypotheticals.. It would really help us to determine what's right or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also like everyone said. This guy is going to spiral with his humanity and he is super easy to defeat in combat or out of combat. Having a defense of 0 is really bad ...<br /> <br /> <br /> I have a question.. Even if something says it does lethal, vampires downgrade to bashing. I think that is true for fighting styles? Your fist did bashing before but now your fist can do lethal with such and such merit... Doesn't it still just do bashing to a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:21:48-07:00","id":917335,"title":"","content":"Altheletics or not everyone is open for sneak attack in that regard. And the vampire slaying style is either on his list or one of the first things he is aiming for. Along with quick draw. <br /> <br /> And of course there are going to averages amongst vampire stats. On average unless you're focusing in that particular path your dice pools for that will fall into an average. You're talking about specialisation and applying that to every aspect of every vampire. But 'most' vampires will get to X level in Y area and then focus on what their character rocks at.<br /> <br /> 25% chance of failure when taking on someone vastly more powerful than yourself isn't terrible. In fact it's amazing. The terrible bit is trying to take on that person in the first place.<br /> <br /> I think you're mistaking this characters intention. He does not play like a crazy murder hobo. He is also fully capable in a fight without going for the sac defence. Shiv also doesn't have to be a literal shiv, it's a 0 damage rated weapon. Which could be bladed. <br /> <br /> Kindred Dueling as mentioned was either on his list or an early purchase. But at any rate it's not going to take long for him to cover most weaknesses you've pointed out.<br /> <br /> In scenario 1. He isn't a crazy murder hobo. He wouldn't go 1v3. <br /> <br /> In 2 using cheap shot is an added bonus. He still has a lot of combat potential even without that. If it does pull off however he kills someone if it would make sense to tactically. <br /> <br /> 3 basically agree, firebombing works but it isn't at all subtle.<br /> <br /> 4 the grappler is dead or stunned before even getting an action. Called shot to the head I believe does this?.on that many dice it's almost impossible to miss. <br /> <br /> So basically given your rather common scenario picking up Kindred fighting and not being an idiotic murder hobo 1v3 let's him win in all the scenarios he can win in. <br /> <br /> Now I know nothing of werewolves the book is on order so I can't defend this one and have no idea what purity is and also no idea what is occurring in terms of actions. But once again id go with the sneak attack head shot. And wouldn't that be 10 bashing not 10 lethal or is that a special werewolf rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:02:48-07:00","id":917407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917335#post917335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altheletics or not everyone is open for sneak attack in that regard. And the vampire slaying style is either on his list or one of the first things he is aiming for. Along with quick draw.</div> </div> </div> </div> You CANNOT use the Vampire Dueling style. You need edged weapons, and neither shiv nor punching daggers qualify - they're both designed as thrusting weapons, not cutting ones. The techniques do not work together. Period. And he cannot move away from using those weapons, because that's the only way he qualifies to use Street Fighting and Light Weaposn together. <br /> <br /> As for weaponry dodge? Its worthless if you don't have a weapon out. That's huge. If you're caught without a weapon out, you do not have anything worthwhile in Defense until your turn, even with Quick Draw. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course there are going to averages amongst vampire stats. </div> </div> </div> You're might argue that there is an so-called average Daeva, average Venture, average Gangrel, but average vampire? That's utterly meaningless, because vampires as a whole run a large variety of stats. A so-called &quot;average&quot; Gangrel or Ventrue is going to have much more health than a Mehket. Meanwhile, an &quot;average&quot; Deava is going to have Celerity, so that needs to be figured in, while an &quot;average&quot; Nosferatu will have Obfuscate instead. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 25% chance of failure when taking on someone vastly more powerful than yourself isn't terrible. </div> </div> </div> I'm getting the feeling you're not listening to us when we tell you that your numbers are wrong. You're trying to convince us that this build is somehow awesome, and we're telling you that you are mistaken. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you're mistaking this characters intention. </div> </div> </div> Nope. I don't think we are. I think that you are overestimating your character and possess a lack of understanding of the rules. You are constantly talking about &quot;future purchases&quot; when that is utterly meaningless. Here and now, your character in question may very well not survive until later. <br /> <br /> You are trying to convince us its an awesome thing, when its really not. There's really nothing more to say. Its a one trick pony with a bad trick. Even when all the situation is in your character's favor (which is very likely to not be), there's a high chance of being slaughtered in turn. The whole point of my example is the sheer number of situations where your character would be FUBAR, and the sheer difficulty of achiving a situation where he could operate as intended, and yet still get effed up. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I know nothing of werewolves the book is on order so I can't defend this one and have no idea what purity is and also no idea what is occurring in terms of actions. But once again id go with the sneak attack head shot. And wouldn't that be 10 bashing not 10 lethal or is that a special werewolf rule? </div> </div> </div> Oh, I said it was lethal. But werewolves don't care. They heal, then eat your face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T10:08:15-07:00","id":917409,"title":"","content":"Two Handed Style allows you to reflexively add your Weapon Rating as general Armor Rating that pretty much cannot be bypassed by called shots. This style also allows you to increase your weapon rating by removing dice from your attack pool, and reduces your opponent's Defense by, again, Weapon Rating. As long as your Sherriff is wielding his sword, or chair, or cleaning mop, he can get pretty big &quot;fuck off&quot; armor. That's why Gangrel with high Resilence and big stick actually works in game as it does in imagery.<br /> <br /> Called shots to the head don't instant kill. There is no instant kill called shot in the game.<br /> <br /> BTW, people, remember that you buy social stuff and mental stuff and physical stuff from different pools. Being a combat monster doesn't make him instantly dumb, that's one of major things in CofD - you don't have to be terrible at something to be good at something, even very good.<br /> <br /> Dude picks higher of his Wits and Dex due to Street Fighting, it's first or second dot allows you to do that.<br /> <br /> Merit he is using is a vampire slaying merit that specifically does lethal damage to vampires. It's the point of the merit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, your biggest problem seems to be Kindred Dueling style, which breaks the spine of Vampire combat - Vampire combat is supposed to be Bashing, and going past Bashing requires either great dedication (keeping kicking that bloodied corpse of a guy until he turns into a dust level of dedication), or pulling out &quot;forbidden&quot; tricks - fire and such. Low lethality of common violence is important for the brutality of the setting, and using that kindred dueling style is kinda like pulling out flamethrowers constantly. If you don't want this level of escalation, ban the Kindred Dueling. It really, really distorts the way kindred combat is played; it's a merit that can turn a mortal into kindred killing machine.<br /> <br /> BTW, I think that discussion about Street Fighting here is pointless, because Street Fighting isn't actually really needed for his combo, he can do fine without it. The problem is Kindred Dueling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:05:54-07:00","id":917570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917407#post917407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You CANNOT use the Vampire Dueling style. You need edged weapons, and neither shiv nor punching daggers qualify - they're both designed as thrusting weapons, not cutting ones. The techniques do not work together. Period. And he cannot move away from using those weapons, because that's the only way he qualifies to use Street Fighting and Light Weaposn together. <br /> <br /> As for weaponry dodge? Its worthless if you don't have a weapon out. That's huge. If you're caught without a weapon out, you do not have anything worthwhile in Defense until your turn, even with Quick Draw. <br /> You're might argue that there is an so-called average Daeva, average Venture, average Gangrel, but average vampire? That's utterly meaningless, because vampires as a whole run a large variety of stats. A so-called &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; Gangrel or Ventrue is going to have much more health than a Mehket. Meanwhile, an &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; Deava is going to have Celerity, so that needs to be figured in, while an &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; Nosferatu will have Obfuscate instead. <br /> <br /> I'm getting the feeling you're not listening to us when we tell you that your numbers are wrong. You're trying to convince us that this build is somehow awesome, and we're telling you that you are mistaken. <br /> <br /> Nope. I don't think we are. I think that you are overestimating your character and possess a lack of understanding of the rules. You are constantly talking about &amp;quot;future purchases&amp;quot; when that is utterly meaningless. Here and now, your character in question may very well not survive until later. <br /> <br /> You are trying to convince us its an awesome thing, when its really not. There's really nothing more to say. Its a one trick pony with a bad trick. Even when all the situation is in your character's favor (which is very likely to not be), there's a high chance of being slaughtered in turn. The whole point of my example is the sheer number of situations where your character would be FUBAR, and the sheer difficulty of achiving a situation where he could operate as intended, and yet still get effed up. <br /> <br /> Oh, I said it was lethal. But werewolves don't care. They heal, then eat your face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shiv: Your character carries small, concealable weapons for use in a tussle. Rolls to detect the concealed weapon suffer your character\u2019s Weaponry score as a penalty. With the one-dot version, she can conceal a weapon with a 0 damage rating. The two-dot version can conceal a 1 damage rating weapon. Your character may use the Brawl Skill to use this weapon<br /> <br /> small weapons with damage ratings of 0 or 1. So a knife which is an edged weapon will have a damage rating of that. Also a razor blade in a tooth brush is a shiv and an edged weapon. So on both accounts it works.<br /> <br /> Weaponry dodge yes if you're unarmed it has its downsides. it's definitely the achilles heel to this build. <br /> <br /> I am definitely listening to you, but so far bar throwing things that no character would be capable of facing down like an ancient sheriff or 3v1 you've not really given me many things to show this build as inferior. I am NOT saying it's the best build. I am NOT saying it's unbeatable. I am saying that compared to a few hyper specialised combat builds it seems like being able to one shot vampires who should be much stronger than you seems imbalanced to me. That is why I posted here to try and find out if that level of power was commonplace. Or if I was going to have a real issue. I am new to the system I do not know all of the tricks and combos. I've stated that but what I do know is simple math that attacking with 20+ dice vs a defence of 0 has an incredibly high chance of 1 shotting vampires. And even without that he will be able to win a lot of fights.<br /> <br /> The numbers however are not wrong. The whole 50% thing was generalising things to the point where you can assume as he has a fairly good level of skill in that area, other vampires will have a similar level. Unless it is an area they are focusing on. Generalised vs specialised. Unless you're taking on a vampire who has specialised in that area for some reason there will be an average. You can argue that all vampires are special snowflakes to your hearts content but that doesn't make it so. After all stats and skills are in no way exclusive to being a vampire. There are some diciplines that add to skills. But saying that an average doesn't exist is like saying that humans don't have averages.<br /> <br /> And to call future purchases meaningless is tosh really, yes if future purchases involved earning 100xp but we are not talking 100xp not even remotely close. A few merit points is all I've mentioned. And if his character can't survive that long then it's 100% the fault of the player and not the build. I could make a trashcan build that can survive long enough to get that much xp as long as I played it smart. <br /> <br /> And you didn't really list situations... you set up a situation and gave him the options of: <br /> <br /> fight 1v3<br /> Fight 3v3<br /> Break the masquerade <br /> Succeed at a stealth check. <br /> <br /> So the first 'option' you gave assumes he is a stupid murder hobo with no friends. In 2 where he brings friends it's an even fight. Unless he succeeds cheap shotting and makes it 3v2. Assuming the friends you bought are as competent as the ones you're facing that looks like a win to me. 3 is a non-option In 4, well he otks one of them. It's then 3v2 and once again as in example 2 as long as you have competent friends you're laughing. <br /> <br /> So when the situation is in his favour. He wins in all the examples you gave? Really not seeing where your claim of him being in an advantageous position = him slaughtered. As far as the difficulty for being in an advantageous position goes, succeeding on a stealth check id hardly call 'difficult' or requiring immense set up. He can more than hold his own in a regular fight and 1v1 if either stealth or a cheap shot land he kills them.<br /> <br /> I am still dubious about this werewolf thing. Do werewolves get extra health levels from somewhere? Because I'm fairly sure that if werewolf follows the same general theme as vampire they will generally have between 6-10 health boxes. So against most werewolves (bar your i assume specialised one that represents the average werewolf) the 11 levels of damage inflicted kills him before he can heal or do diddly. <br /> <br /> I'm not talking about this guy going up against specialised builds. I'm talking about the average. Which does exist. He isn't unbeatable. Far from it. And I don't think it's a super awesome build. It is a one trick pony. I am simply trying to figure out a baseline for what represents power in this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:12:06-07:00","id":917643,"title":"","content":"Hey, the zweihander Sherriff isn't &quot;an ancient&quot; build. It requires just 4 merit dots to work :P. <br /> <br /> In general, there are two parts to this dude's build that make it strong. First one is Thrust manuever of Light Weapons; it offers great flexibility and potential alpha strike capabilities, because it allows you to spend any number of your Defense to get attack dice. Again, this character doesn't have to bring himself to 0 Defense; he may as well just bump his attack by one or two, to get into sweet range of 5 dice, or use it as a super all out attack when it's tactically plausible. This makes a great ambusher and great duelist tactic as you noticed.<br /> However, this doesn't work as well in normal circumstances; many supernatural creatures in CofD can survive an overwhelming alpha strike. Vampires are pretty good at it; they can reflexively heal up pretty much any tilt you throw at them, due to being able to heal a lot of bashing damage in a single go. A Blood Potency 2 character can instantly get rid of any tilts attached to 4 boxes of bashing damage. This means that a tilt will last 2 rounds at best. <br /> <br /> Again, this whole thing goes south because of Kindred Dueling style. Ability to deal lethal damage in a ecosystem balanced for bashing damage will make things work not as intended. Standard Kindred fight might involve broken bones, snapped jaws, dislocated spines...and a vampire going &quot;fuck, this hurt, you asshole, im out of here&quot;, spending some blood and exiting the scene without any damage, but with a dent in their blood economy.<br /> <br /> Here is a thing - casual violence in Vampire is a thing. Vampires tend to flip out. Game knows that Vampires WILL throw cars at themselves when they got pissed off to settle a dispute. So it had a very difficult dillema to solve - how do you allow this, pretty iconic, behavior to happen regularly without introducing a serious risk of death? The answer they arrived was, I believe, this:<br /> You keep damage brutal and visceral, and embrace the idea of damaging tilts to evoke the gory imagery; however, you downgrade all damage to bashing; this, coupled with massive health bar *and* reflexive way to heal massive amounts of damage ensures that &quot;a lucky crit&quot; issue doesn't exist; there is literally NO WAY to kill someone accidentally. You can't punch another vampire and roll a crit that will kill him. In order to kill someone, you need to have clear killer intent. However, obviously, if it was just this, combat would loose it teeth; without consequences, combat doesn't feel right, and we just removed &quot;characters might die&quot; consequence from combat. So, in order to keep combat not-trivial, LETHAL damage costs more to heal; the point where a Vampire get's punched into Lethal damage is a good warning sign, a signal to stop fighting, because these wounds stop being something you can heal off with just a thought. Then, going into aggravated offers you another warning sign; these wounds won't heal anytime soon; one aggravated damage is enough to stop pretty much anyone from pursuing further conflict, unless it's really dramatic and important. <br /> Of course, these are consequences of Lethal and Aggravated brawls. What are consequences of the casual, vibrant and ecstatic Bashing Brawl? It's easy to heal off, and you won't even remember it 5 minutes later, yes? Isn't it meaningless?<br /> Well, no. Keeping yourself away from Lethal Damage will have a very real consequence - it will put a dent into your blood economy. Casual brawls force you to go and eat, they give you a moment of weakness during your night, they might make you stop and think twice before doing something you planned on doing. It's not a permanent consequence, but a very real, gameplay shaping consequence that allows brutal fighting have a civilized place in bestial nights of the dead. This is why you can really have two vampire friends who regularly flip out and tear each other's arms off and then are all like &quot;uh, dude, im totally sorry about that last week, ok? it was not cool&quot;, and it allows your violent vampire archetype to be viable and fun to play. There aren't many games where you can engage in a joyful, terryfing muscle mash with your favorite NPCs, turning them into bloody meat, and not break the setting or make your character out of place. <br /> <br /> Why I'm talking about this? If your player enjoys violence and combat in games, you might try to persuade him to drop the killer intent; killer intent breaks this whole social contract of &quot;tonight we tear each other's arms off, but tommorow, tommorow we drink together&quot;; it's a funny thing, but while optimizing to kill sounds like a natural thing to do for a combat character, it isn't really the best solution for a character that want's to participate in a lot of combat in Vampire, because the moment where you reach for flamethrower, for Kindred Dueling, and for Claws of the Unholy, you remove yourself from the accepted culture of nightly fight clubbing, and step into &quot;murderer&quot; territory. And when you go into murder territory, game starts to become much more binary; you live or die. In the world of muscle mash? You fight, you win, you lose, you break a bone, you tear off an arm, you go and unlive with it. There are many more possible outcomes in the world of self restrained bashing than in cutthroat lethality. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T21:36:49-07:00","id":917784,"title":"","content":"One of the werewolf forms can heal all lethal and bashing at the start of their turn. I believe that is what they were referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T01:46:15-07:00","id":917866,"title":"","content":"I have a problem with a player's craziness....response....defends player craziness....response....defends player craziness...response...defends player craziness.<br /> <br /> Why did you even ask then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11937-theunknownmourner","name":"TheUnknownMourner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T01:55:10-07:00","id":917869,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11937-theunknownmourner\">TheUnknownMourne</a> </b>I think, the problem is that the qwestion is not about craziness, but the answers are. I mean, we've all are pretty hard used to the concept of Minmax-powergaming being a method of insuring crazy roleplay, but the author sais that the player is not a crazylooner. But such a build needs some <b>honest </b>and appropriate challenge from the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> As I see the problem is:<br /> 1) When it comes to combat, this player plays onepunchman and ends battle before it starts.<br /> 2) If ST finds a serious enemy for this megafighter, then all the rest coterie will be smashed in the first round or has to stay aside.<br /> <br /> So the result is completely ruined combat scenes.<br /> <br /> What to do with it? Well, nothing, I suppose. There is a reason why the player generates such a character, so let him do what he does and have all the consequences: boring combat scenes, precise attention from Kindred. Maybe the Prince will grant him a title of Hound, with all the duties and responsibilities.<br /> <br /> Also less and less Beats in combat. No challenge -- no experience.<br /> <br /> By the way, what the others characters are like? Are they fighters or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-20-2016, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:17:27-07:00","id":918067,"title":"","content":"@WHW yes you're spot on the mark, it's Kindred fighting style that really throws it into overdrive. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11937-theunknownmourner\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11937\" data-vbnamecard=\"11937\">TheUnknownMourner</a> of course I'm defending the player. I'm putting myself in his shoes and comming up with arguments he would make to defend his position. I am all for a discussion with the players before vetoing anything. But that requires I know both sides. By vehemtly arguing how good the build is. And how the rules can be interpreted to support it. And basically playing Devil's advocate I create the kind of discussion that looks at all facets. Rather than just accepting the first resolution that occurs.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6186\" data-vbnamecard=\"6186\">Aleksay</a> pretty much nail on the head here too. I hate telling a player there character is boring or op. They spent the time building it. I would rather try to find a way of giving them a challenge in the area they excel at. But that's obviously difficult when they are quite well stacked in that area. <br /> <br /> And no the other characters are not fighters. Most of them are going to play the long game, set up positions of political power, consolidate that power, and be strong in that way. And I will be awarding beats for creative approaches to situations. Anyone who dominates their way like a bull in a China shop will not learn as much as someone who manipulates and plots. Same goes for combat. If this character just goes on killing sprees he won't be getting much xp compared to the person who is smart about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:35:29-07:00","id":918078,"title":"","content":"Pretty much appreciate your approach, thank you. Well, being SO MUCH ahead in the art of killing this guy deserves to be one of the best fighter of the Domain. That said, he'll obviously be too <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">sticking out like a sore thumb among neonates to be overlooked by elders. Tension escalation will certainly follow. All the most important politicians would like to control such a great tool or to wipe him out. That's just natural way. The combat scenes for him are too simple, but choosing the aims, the propper figures to kill, the propper Kindred to ally with, would be interesting, no?<br /> <br /> As for the rest of the group, then... well, having such an ally, they can dictate their own will to the Domain. Neonates at power, why not? </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:55:05-07:00","id":918126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917869#post917869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But such a build needs some <b>honest </b>and appropriate challenge from the Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>As we've been trying to illustrate, the character build is insanely easy to challenge because it's a one-trick pony built on trying to alpha-strike against zero Defense targets; which is actually an incredibly poor choice of combat tactics for vampires if they'd planning on doing anything other than offing minor characters. Even if there aren't many ways to gain Defense immune to sneak attacks, Cheap Shot, or whatever, there's still tons of ways to not get harmed. And this doesn't require unbeatable combat monsters that can out alpha-strike this PC, or casually kill vampires in single hits without losing their own defense. There are so many options that don't result in your #2 that results in a TPK; esp. because the rest of the coterie doesn't have to stand by this PC if he gets in over his head with the wrong enemy.<br /> <br /> This isn't D&amp;D where anything you fight is 99% of the time Evil and out to mindlessly kill the party. If this PC pisses off the wrong people and gets whooped for it, the rest of the coterie can hold up their hands and say, &quot;Dude had it coming, we're sorry,&quot; and there's little reason to beat them too. They might not get away without some penalties, but why kill them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=918067#post918067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... of course I'm defending the player. I'm putting myself in his shoes and comming up with arguments he would make to defend his position. I am all for a discussion with the players before vetoing anything. But that requires I know both sides. By vehemtly arguing how good the build is. And how the rules can be interpreted to support it. And basically playing Devil's advocate I create the kind of discussion that looks at all facets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but there's also a point where this goes too far. If you were my player pushing this hard, I'd be at the point where I don't think you want a conversation/discussion to find an agreeable solution, but that you just want to have your power-combo (and stack more on it later). You've pointed out all the ways the rules could be interpreted in one direction, but no reasons <i>why</i> an ST should rule that way instead of far more sensible things (like not allowing Weaponry and Brawl Fighting Style Merits stack unless the rules say they do).<br /> <br /> If you're defending the player, address that issue, not the viability of various rules interpretation, because that's the discussion to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hate telling a player there character is boring or op. </div> </div> </div>Sometimes we have to. That's one of the responsibilities we take on when we ST. Players make characters that aren't always good for the rest of the game (legal builds or not), and having such a character involved is ultimately unfun for you, likely unsatisfying for your player, and of questionable fun for the rest.<br /> <br /> In the future, maybe something to do is to make sure you've talked to your players before they make PCs? It's not a 100% solution, but I've found it heads off a lot of these things because they haven't built anything yet, so you can set/negotiate some expectations before they do. If you say, before anyone makes a PC, that this isn't going to be a combat heavy game and that most violence will be done via the Down &amp; Dirty rules rather than full combat if it comes up, players can still make violence oriented PCs, but know not to dump tons of dots into Fighting Merits or worry about squeezing out every last bit of advantage from the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:43:19-07:00","id":918277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=917332#post917332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have a question.. Even if something says it does lethal, vampires downgrade to bashing. I think that is true for fighting styles? Your fist did bashing before but now your fist can do lethal with such and such merit... Doesn't it still just do bashing to a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright this was never fully answered. Someone said yes, because of Kindred fighting style... which I know for Kindred fighting style. It specifically says that it does &quot; Lethal damage to Kindred instead of bashing&quot; it specifically includes them... But there were other fighting styles mentioned in this thread Streetfighting and light weapon.<br /> <br /> the 5th in Light weapon states : &quot; If the attack roll succeeds, the attack causes one point of aggravated damage &quot; is that still aggravated to a vampire? I would think not...<br /> <br /> I am just going to add in Heavy... &quot; any character moving into your character\u2019s proximity suffers one lethal damage&quot; I also dont think this is lethal either because kindred downgrade unless it otherwise says so ( Like Kindred fighting style)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T16:02:39-07:00","id":918286,"title":"","content":"What counters this character and isn't hyper-specialized or is at least believable? Numbers, grappling, tilts, long-ranged gunfights, Obfuscate, Celerity, mind control, anything that auto-counters stealth (like Auspex arguably). Some longer thoughts below.<br /> <br /> The character can indeed oneshot things. Make sure his backstory is consistent with this.<br /> <br /> The problem with hyper-specialized characters are challenging them, keeping the other characters involved, keeping the other characters relevant, and the rocket tag effect.<br /> <br /> You're going to want to avoid challenging the player with high-defense opponents because then the other characters will feel useless. Also because the system is offense-oriented, especially when you go supernatural. It's much easier to get offense than defense, there's no way you can compete with the insane amount of dice Thrust gives Munchkin McNinja from Light Weapons style.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you can't really avoid the rocket tag effect. Combat *should* be lethal in a setting and system like this. The PCs should try to only take fights that they think they can win. This naturally lends itself to making a campaign non-combat oriented so that when combat does occur, it's a big moment. By taking this approach, you're already naturally dealing with the combat monster, because he's reduced to his secondary roles of Larceny and Stealth to support the coterie. It also makes McNinja feel special, because the rare thing is his domain (unless he's a D&amp;D player who expects combat all the time)<br /> <br /> One way you can occasionally let the other characters feel powerful is to give them access too allies via their social maneuvering. If they talk the allies into helping them for a deadly encounter, give them near-full control of the character in question. (Basically access to temporary retainers/mentors/allies)<br /> <br /> Unless the coterie does something insanely ambitious in the beginning, you should def have McNinja or anyone else who has a specialized character kick ass in their domains in the first few sessions of the game. That way it emerges who is great at what. Once they have their moment in the spotlight and character roles are solidified...<br /> <br /> Now let's talk about challenging McNinja. You seem to discount disciplines. This is a supernatural game, at some point fighting actual vampires and not their human pawns is going to happen.<br /> <br /> You seem to also discount numbers. If the character doesn't want to 1v3 or the party doesn't want to say 5v8 or 5v10 or whatever, it's your job to incentivize this or have their goals fail as a result of not wanting to take on the potentially deadly encounter. In superhero games for example, a scenario is often not about beating the bad guy, but trying to both beat him *and* save innocents in the process. Come up with appropriate scenarios why the party would want to at least consider taking on superior numbers in Vampire, such as getting a guarded McGuffin for the Prince surrounded by lots of people.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Threat</b><br /> Gangs of Mooks - Raw numbers and sheer # of attacks are a great way to lower Defense and a big incentive to not All-Out Attack. A low-level example if a bunch of gangers sitting around eating shit, protecting a McGuffin. Medium level example would be a security force all getting together around a McGuffin when they notice everyone is getting oneshotted and not reporting in because McNinja is killing everything.<br /> <br /> Badass Normal - A very perceptive mortal can probably spot McNinja, allowing him to radio a larger group of mortals, ruining any chance of further stealth. A legendary wrestler type thrown in the mix can probably grapple Munchkin McNinja, at least until he gets Double Jointed. Maybe give these guys Quick Reflexes so they have a chance of going first.<br /> <br /> 1 or 2 snipers - Maybe have a sniper or two guard a location. It'd be a nice, non-lethal surprise for the party if they didn't do their legwork or properly scout.<br /> <br /> He Got Away! - A surviving mortal or whatver can get away easily if he gets to a car in time or maybe just the party doesn't have access to Celerity, chasing power, or Survival for tracking. Appropriate consequences ensue.<br /> <br /> Social Faux Pax - The Prince or an important frou-frou douchey NPC invites the whole coterie to have tea with him, L5R style. McNinja fumbles the social rolls and a potential ally becomes distant, or even hostile.<br /> <br /> Role Reversal - The party is out of commission or separated for some reason and time is a constraint. McNinja is forced to go be The Face (or whatever other role), likely screwing things up in the process<br /> <br /> <b>Medium Threat</b><br /> Hidden Badass - The coterie takes on a threat they think they can take on. They kill the Big Guy or the Obvious Leader of the encounter. Surprisingly, after the oneshot occur, it turns out there's a badass in the mix that happens to hard counter McNinja, like a vampire grappler. I don't recommend doing this too often. If you do do it, fluff it as his muscles have been wirey and hidden beneath his clothes, anime-style, Bruce Lee style. Allow decent Perception checks beforehand to spot this.<br /> <br /> Ninja vs Ninja - McNinja is pretty good at sneaking around. Have another ninja come after him and grapple him when he's alone. To make this dramatic, you can have it be while the party is a few turns away, so they get there in time to save him.<br /> <br /> Alucard vs Coterie/McNinja - A high Celerity ranged character can kite the party and put on some serious damage. McNinja can't do his Light Weapons Thrust shenanigans to someone he can't reach.<br /> <br /> He Got Away... Again! - With access to Celerity and Obfuscate, it can be easy for bad guys to get away unless the party does amazing legwork and has good teamwork (or insane alphastrike potential)<br /> <br /> Kindred Duel - Design a rival, maybe more powerful, basically just for him and railroad him (if he's down for it) into a non-lethal duel. Use say, wooden knives. Game it as basically a normal combat but with no actual damage being done, first one to put the other guy in fake-torpor wins... Or just have a judge, if that doesn't make sense. Maybe even have him use a very similar build to the player's character, and namedrop him when Important Vampires are first impressed by the coterie (&quot;McNinja's cold edge reminds me of McRival... did McRival sire you, McNinja?&quot; and such gossip like that) Later in the campaign, have the rival hunt McNinja. Since he knows how rocket-taggy his own character is, there'll be heavy paranoia for a while.<br /> <br /> <b>High Threat</b><br /> Any of the specialized builds mentioned in this thread. Also, any of the general advice mentioned (for example, maybe his reputation begins to precede him, Hunters are put on to him, I dunno, anything.) I mention grappling a lot because biting is a big part of Vampire (so it's common) and frenzied biters can auto-grapple and grappling is a weakness of the build (at least, until Double Jointed)<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> That said, if you truly don't want to say &quot;no&quot; to the character but still wanna nerf him, you can resort to house rules. If I were to go this route, I'd swap Thrust (Level 2 Light Weapons) with the level 4 or 5 Light Weapons merit, forcing the character to invest heavily to have access to obnoxious dice. I'd also increase the cost of Cheap Shot and Defensive Combat by 1. You could also maybe nerf Kindred dueling somehow. All of these things would delay his build heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","user":"Captain Shoe","date":". 06-20-2016, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:02:37-07:00","id":918320,"title":"","content":"I'd just say none of the three fighting styles in question stack in any way. Even if there was no potentially OP fighting style involved. Seems silly to me to try to employ three maneuvers on the same turn in any given situation, except perhaps when said maneuvers are largely passive.<br /> <br /> I don't consider a shiv a weapon that relies on finesse, especially if/when you're using Brawl to use the weapon (which you'd have to use to use any Street Fighting technique). Second, I'd say carving requires a sword. <br /> <br /> Punch daggers are illegal in most of the US, so he'd have to expend some effort to get those. Actual shivs I'd argue aren't appropriate for any fighting styles as written. Daggers though, sure. That's all on you and how you run your games.<br /> <br /> Second, your guy's max pool is 26 or something to that effect if everything goes right, which averages out at 11 damage. Any character with 5 dots in Resilience blocks more than half of that. Then they get a chance to get this guy in a grapple, or a frienzied attack. Or just a similar attack with a bunch of vigor. Throw 6 xp on any starting character (if in-clan) and they can have 5 dots of Resilience. Neither implausible nor uncommon for a character who wants to fight. Cheapshot isn't likely to work again, and on the chance it does, said opponent would likely still survive<br /> <br /> The 5th dot of the Close Combat fighting style disarms an opponent more or less automatically, and again, completely stymies this attack.<br /> <br /> As does Celerity. Which has been mentioned, but when/if the character gets Celerity himself, winning that Clash of Wills isn't any less likely than him winning his Cheapshot roll. That's two rolls he has to succeed at before he can even get his OP fighting maneuver off the ground. If his opponent has more Celerity or a higher BP, they'll likely win that Clash of Wills, which leaves our guy very vulnerable at this point having Thrusted and sacrificed his defense (assuming in this scenario that he's sacrificed all of it). At which point he can be grappled or just flat hit with a similarly devastating assault.<br /> <br /> If he makes enough enemies, an Assassin with Obfuscate and some Carving and/or Vigor can do what he does with more reliability.<br /> <br /> Then we throw in other characters using Obfuscate and Protean, with more wily ways to win battles and it becomes even more complicated. Swarm Form, Mist Form. A frenzied Gangrel with Claws of the Unholy, Horrid Talons or Barbed Hands will wreck him in a Grapple, which they could apply on attack. The BP Bonus from Frenzying and a higher focus on brawl would leave him very disadvantaged, as he's unlikely to win the grapple.<br /> <br /> Or a Ventrue with Dominate and a horde of manservants, bodyguards, ghouls, etc. willing to die for him. 10 dots of merits translated into 10 dots of retainer/protection is just as effective as a grab bag of fighting styles, if not moreso. God forbid he has more. Or a Nosferatu playing with his head, can easily just sending him fleeing from a battle. Lashing out can subdue him. <br /> <br /> And if you want to put him in his place, just throw him against a vampire with 10 more xp than he has. Maybe a couple extra BP. <br /> <br /> As far as winning the cheapshot roll, as has already been mentioned, acute senses, danger sense, auspex, etc. There are a dozen ways to beat a 7 die roll that degrades with each attempt. <br /> <br /> So his combination is powerful, but not nearly as strong as you seem to think. And honestly, if you're so worried about it, just throw in two characters with the exact same spread and throw them at him. Or one with a dot more Vigor. You're the ST, it should be laughably easy to challenge your PCs. You can do anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:53:48-07:00","id":918347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=918286#post918286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to want to avoid challenging the player with high-defense opponents because then the other characters will feel useless. Also because the system is offense-oriented, especially when you go supernatural. It's much easier to get offense than defense, there's no way you can compete with the insane amount of dice Thrust gives Munchkin McNinja from Light Weapons style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of good stuff, though I have a few issues with this paragraph:<br /> <br /> 1) High Defense characters are actually something the non-combat helpers can be useful for: each attack (fail or not) reduces Defense (baring Merits/Powers). It's one of the reasons that while 2e has upped Defense significantly from 1e, numbers remain the most brutal factor. A high Defense oriented enemy has to choose to maintain their Defense against major enemies (how do they know who at first?) and let low combat characters get free hits on them, or let their Defense drop as minor attacks they can easily fend off leave them open to a big hitter.<br /> <br /> 2) You can actually compete with Thrust. Armed Defense great for stomping it down - remembering that Dodge uses a base dice pool of double base Defense and then adds any additional bonuses. A character with no powers, and not maxing out Dex and Wits, can still easily get up to ~18 Dodge dice, and then apply all sorts of counter attacks with the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:10:29-07:00","id":918765,"title":"","content":"Oh the build is very easy to challenge in a way that's completely unrewarding for all parties involved. Basically by putting him in situations where nobody could win. It's like sending a high level assassin after a social player. What I want is to offer a rewarding challenge for the player and stacking the odds so he loses as per your examples really isn't the way to go about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11106\" data-vbnamecard=\"11106\">Captain Shoe</a> thankyou that was an incredibly useful post. I will definitly be making use of those scenarios. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> the problem with defence pimping is that a single effect that sets your defence to 0 completely stops any and every effect you've purchased to up your defence. This is the big thing that to me threw up red flags with his build. Normally vs a character like this id make a high defence character to offer a challenge so that he would only successfully hit say 30% of the time. However with set defence to 0 being a thing in the game it can make that hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11995-wunderkid","name":"Wunderkid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:32:27-07:00","id":918782,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem may be that the OP wants to have combat operate in an epic fantasy style brawl, and not the short violent mess that the CofD uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:24:07-07:00","id":918802,"title":"","content":"The Kindred Fighting Style ability Carving doesn't seem to allow you to turn all your damage to Lethal. It says, 'When Carving, your weapon's damage rating deals lethal damage to Kindred instead of bashing.' Later, specifically p179, it explains, 'A weapon's damage rating adds bonus successes to a successful attack roll.' Using weapons available with Shiv only allows for a maximum of 1 Lethal damage in that fashion, not counting wrap-around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:36:55-07:00","id":918807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=918765#post918765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh the build is very easy to challenge in a way that's completely unrewarding for all parties involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really... especially if you challenge the character outside of direct one-on-one confrontations.<br /> <br /> If you're facing off against a group, a non-combat Dominate or Nightmare specialist can just start sending non-vampire combatants running and massively change the course of the fight without lifting a fist (and don't have to invest nearly as much into being good at it against non-vampire lackeys, and even vampires can't defend against everything).<br /> <br /> I don't see how using the non-combat oriented PCs with one assumes investments in Disciplines of some sort to use social/mental oriented Disciplines to clear away lackeys and leave the main opponent to the combat heavy (which they can aid with as well) would be unrewarding.<br /> <br /> Also, reward versatility. If this character is a master of weapons, stealth, and subterfuge, reward them separately rather than only when they can squeeze out a mega-combo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I want is to offer a rewarding challenge for the player and stacking the odds so he loses as per your examples really isn't the way to go about it. </div> </div> </div>He only loses if he sticks on that one option available to him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..the problem with defence pimping is that a single effect that sets your defence to 0 completely stops any and every effect you've purchased to up your defence. This is the big thing that to me threw up red flags with his build. Normally vs a character like this id make a high defence character to offer a challenge so that he would only successfully hit say 30% of the time. However with set defence to 0 being a thing in the game it can make that hard. </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that you're basically saying, &quot;I'm comfortable making an even opponent against one proficiency, but not against three, so when he uses all three I can't challenge him.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;Set Defense to 0&quot; moves are not free or automatic. If you're not going to put in characters that can resist them, this character will steamroll. If all your NPCs and Resolve and Composure 1, don't expect a Dominate/Majesty/Nightmare user to not walk all over them too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T10:10:33-07:00","id":920437,"title":"","content":"I also had a situation with two PCs atacking a Daeva NPC without any plan.<br /> Daeva just used Majesty against the strongest one, and asked him to beat the shit off the second. The condition was resolved in the next turn (with the second PC having all-but-one health cells filled with bashing), but the Daeva in qwestion had already ran away with Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 06-24-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:22:30-07:00","id":921548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wunderkid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd#post916672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. One of the players has come up with a build that nets him around the 25 dice to attack while denying the opponents defence. This is through a combination of high strength, Dex, weaponry, vigour and the light weapons merit which allows you to sac your defence and add it to your attack. Cheap shot to deny them their defence if his stealth attack doesn't pan out.<br /> <br /> Street fighting 3 let's him inflict the knocked down tilt which makes a person lose their action. And with this many dice he can comfortably aim for even the smallest gap in armor. And then the Kindred fighting style thrown in on top to be able to inflict lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So I firstly just wanted to make sure this was legit. Because it does seem absolutely insane being able to aim for the eye slit vs full plate still be on 20+ dice, and knock them down, blind them, and deny them defence and armor. And also how you would challenge them? Are there any merits/powers that would allow you to keep your defence when an effect says deny?</div> </div> </div> </div>You throw a molotov on him, watch him get caught on fire and die in like 3 or 4 turns as he tries to rid himself of the on fire condition,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:55:46-07:00","id":921562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/916672-a-few-newbie-questions-vtr-2nd?p=921548#post921548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You throw a molotov on him, watch him get caught on fire and die in like 3 or 4 turns as he tries to rid himself of the on fire condition,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best combat tactic I've seen suggested so far on this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}